        "original_id": "b8bbe880-7c10-5fe4-9d28-c3fd665adb77",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Companies: Selfridges, Harrods, Jack O'Shea's\n- Places: Oxford Street, London, UK, Qatar\n- Topics: flagship stores, ownership, retail contracts, ethical code, foie gras\n\nFacts:\n- Selfridges opened its flagship store on Oxford Street in London on 15 March 1909.\n- Selfridges' Oxford Street flagship store is the second largest shop in the UK after Harrods.\n- Harrods is owned by the state of Qatar.\n- Jack O'Shea's was formerly located in Selfridges.\n- Selfridges terminated Jack O'Shea's contract in 2012 after Jack O'Shea's broke the store's ethical code by selling foie gras.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
